course: dictionary
lesson: 9400
title: One word, three jobs
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one you need. Look at the words around the word. «The taiga is mostly spruce, pine, fir and larch.» Pine and fir are trees, so spruce must be a tree too.
explain: Spruce can also be an adjective, a describing word. «Spruce» means neat, clean and smart in appearance. If someone looks spruce before a party, they look tidy and ready to be seen.
explain: Spruce up is a phrase, and it is a verb, an action word. To spruce up a room is to make it look neater and smarter. Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have chosen the right meaning.
fact: Spruce can be a noun, an adjective or a verb, so its meaning depends on the sentence.
fact: A spruce is a tall evergreen tree with short needles and hanging cones.
fact: Spruce wood is light, and it is used for paper and guitars.
fact: «Spruce» as an adjective means neat, clean and smart in appearance.
fact: «The cone shape of a spruce lets heavy snow slide off instead of breaking the branches.»
exercise: «The taiga is mostly spruce, pine, fir and larch.» What is a spruce in this sentence? | A neat and smart person | *A tall evergreen tree | A petrol station in Australia | A cold, deep lake
exercise: Mum wants to spruce up the kitchen before the guests arrive. What does spruce up mean? | To make it wet and grey | To cut it down | *To make it neater and smarter | To paint it black
exercise: «Evergreen trees, like pine and spruce, keep their needles all year.» What kind of trees are pine and spruce? | *Evergreen trees | Types of snow | Lakes that freeze in winter | Deciduous trees that drop leaves in autumn
test: «Narrow waxy needles lose little water and survive frost.» What are the needles in this sentence? | Small, cold stones | Sharp rocks on the hill | *Thin, pointed leaves of the spruce tree | Long, soft ropes used for boats
test: After her bath, Ava looked spruce in her clean, ironed clothes. What does spruce mean? | Tired and sleepy | Lost in a forest | *Neat, clean and smart | Wet and muddy
exam: Which sentence uses spruce to mean a tree? | Her spruce clothes were ironed and clean | *The cone-shaped spruce stood tall in the snow | The boys spruced themselves up for the party | Please spruce up your bedroom before Gran visits
